# macOS-only Ghostty overrides. Ghostty loads ~/.config/ghostty/config on
# every platform, then on macOS also loads this file on top (see the comment
# at the top of active/shared/.config/ghostty/config). Deliberately does NOT
# repeat the `config-file = ...` theme-include line from that file: doing so
# would make Ghostty load the same path twice and refuse it with "cycle
# detected".

# Ghostty hardcodes a macOS-only default ("natural text editing" keybinds,
# see loadDefaultFiles in upstream src/config/Config.zig) that sends
# Alt+Left/Right as ESC b / ESC f (legacy word-navigation) instead of the
# normal fixterm Alt+Arrow CSI sequence, so herdr's previous_tab/next_tab
# keys (alt+left/alt+right, see active/shared/.config/herdr/config.toml)
# never see the keystroke. Alt+Up/Down has no such default, so it already
# reaches herdr untouched. Ghostty's own upstream comment names `unbind` as
# the way back to fixterm encoding, so use that rather than guessing at the
# raw CSI bytes ourselves.
keybind = alt+left=unbind
keybind = alt+right=unbind
